From 322117b8dccf9446d0ede57e651802e78e15dcc6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 18:42:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] hw: a whole-file save writes the file and reports what the
 checker found

Why: the hardware text store refused a whole-file save (Config page Save,
Undo, history restore, set_controls text=) when hwconf::validate found an
error the current file did not have, even where every reader accepts the
file (for example a key set twice: the readers take the later line).
Original Apertar 1.6.0 checks a whole-file save only for empty, 256 KiB
and NUL bytes, then writes it (saveHardwareConfigFile,
src/ApertarCoreApp.cpp:5323-5386@upstream-1.6.0); the readers keep their
defaults for what they cannot use (HW-12). The Check button also said
"Save is refused until the errors are fixed."

What: HardwareConfigStore::saveLocked works out the new errors only for
key edits, so only a key edit (set_controls set.<section>.<key>=) is still
refused when it adds an error; the Controls page writes keys the operator
did not type. A whole-file save is written and its ok reply carries the
issues and the error count, as before. StoreFlags::force is documented as
key edits only. The Check sentence now reads "Save writes the file anyway;
the readers skip what they cannot use."

Tested: check_core.sh both builds and the host tests pass. Simulate:
POST /api/config with d17=capture twice in [gpio_buttons] returns ok:true,
written:true, one duplicate_key issue, and the file holds the text; a key
edit set.gpio_buttons.d18=no_such_action is refused with "Not saved: 1 new
error." and the file is unchanged. Headless Chromium: Check on that text
ends in the new sentence; Save writes it and lists the issue. Pi: nothing
to check, no hardware path changes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NEFc1w7Y8dcyiV489BiwMr
---
 src/hardware/HardwareConfigStore.cpp | 5 ++++-
 src/hardware/HardwareConfigStore.hpp | 2 +-
 src/web/WebControlPage.cpp           | 2 +-
 3 files changed, 6 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/hardware/HardwareConfigStore.cpp b/src/hardware/HardwareConfigStore.cpp
index 872f166..f91ad58 100644
--- a/src/hardware/HardwareConfigStore.cpp
+++ b/src/hardware/HardwareConfigStore.cpp
@@ -333,7 +333,10 @@ StoreResult HardwareConfigStore::saveLocked(const std::string &base, const std::
         result.error = "Script paths are changed over ssh, not here.";
         return result;
     }
-    result.newErrors = hwconf::newErrors(hwconf::validate(current, facts), result.issues);
+    // A whole-file save is written whatever the checker finds, as in 1.6.0: the readers skip what they cannot use
+    // and the reply names the issues. A key edit that adds an error is refused: the page writes keys nobody typed.
+    if (edits)
+        result.newErrors = hwconf::newErrors(hwconf::validate(current, facts), result.issues);
     if (!result.newErrors.empty() && !flags.force) {
         result.code = "errors";
         result.error = "Not saved: " + std::to_string(result.newErrors.size()) + " new error" +
diff --git a/src/hardware/HardwareConfigStore.hpp b/src/hardware/HardwareConfigStore.hpp
index 6d1f8c6..0ed034e 100644
--- a/src/hardware/HardwareConfigStore.hpp
+++ b/src/hardware/HardwareConfigStore.hpp
@@ -16,7 +16,7 @@ namespace apertar::hardware {
 
 struct StoreFlags {
     bool dryRun = false;        // work out everything, write nothing
-    bool force = false;         // save although the new text has errors the current one does not
+    bool force = false;         // key edits only: save although the edit adds errors
     bool backup = false;        // also keep <file>.bak: WebUI and core.py saves only
     bool confirmMerge = false;  // a stale text save that merged onto the current file: write it now
     bool trusted = false;       // Core's own code (the IMU): the easy-mode key checks are skipped
diff --git a/src/web/WebControlPage.cpp b/src/web/WebControlPage.cpp
index 4075c43..a2e14d3 100644
--- a/src/web/WebControlPage.cpp
+++ b/src/web/WebControlPage.cpp
@@ -18882,7 +18882,7 @@ std::string_view webControlPageHtml()
       }
       const errors = found.filter((issue) => issue.error).length;
       showConfigIssues("Checked: " + errors + (errors === 1 ? " error" : " errors") + ", " + (found.length - errors) +
-        (found.length - errors === 1 ? " warning" : " warnings") + (errors ? ". Save is refused until the errors are fixed." : "."), found);
+        (found.length - errors === 1 ? " warning" : " warnings") + (errors ? ". Save writes the file anyway; the readers skip what they cannot use." : "."), found);
     }
 
     // T43: the lines that differ between the loaded file and the editor (a longest-common-subsequence line diff),
-- 
